# Commit messages

After finishing a substantive change (code, tests, docs, CI), always end with a
suggested commit message the user can copy—even when they did not ask to commit.

- Exactly one line (no body, no blank line after the subject)
- Match this repo’s style: conventional commits (`fix:`, `feat:`, `test:`, `docs:`, `ci:`, `refactor:`)
- Keep it short and why-focused
- Do not create the commit unless the user explicitly asks
